  four WorkflowFieldUpdate), are the set the org validated in reports/mock-deploy/2026-10-02T18-04-04Z
  (MOCK-DEPLOY-M4 run 3: 43 ok, 2 expected errors, see N4-F-06 below).

  M2-S04 IS A MEMBER. plan.json steps[M4-S04].inputs still lists "M2-S04 (excluded, blocked)".
  That prose predates the 2026-09-15 unblock; acceptance test 5, amended 2026-10-02T18:52:18Z, says
  the rule ships exactly once, M2-S04 is documented, and MOCK-DEPLOY-M2 run 3 validated it. The
  amended test and the step's real status win over the stale input note.

  ONE FILE, TWO REQUESTS. This file names every member, but it cannot be validated or deployed as
  one request: a Report cannot be validated in the same deployment as the new ReportType it names
  (N4-F-06, MOCK-DEPLOY-M4 run 3). deploy-order.md section 4 lists the two requests member by member:
  request 1 is this file without Report Enterprise_Sales/Open_Enterprise_Pipeline_By_Stage and
  Dashboard Enterprise_Sales/Enterprise_Pipeline; request 2 is those two members.

  A DEPLOY MANIFEST, NEVER A RETRIEVE MANIFEST. It names Profile and PermissionSet beside
  CustomObject. Retrieved together, the object rewrites the profile files
  (admin/object-creation-and-design gotchas.md Gotcha 10; artefacts/M2-S02/deploy-order.md section 4).

  FOUR FILES MUST BE CHANGED IN THE DEPLOY COPY BEFORE A REAL DEPLOY, and none of those changes is
  made here: the OpportunityStage merge, the Opportunity Products related list on both layouts, the
  dashboard runningUser, and the Opportunity object-file merge. deploy-order.md section 2.

  Member forms: object-qualified for CustomField, BusinessProcess, RecordType, ValidationRule and
  ApprovalProcess; Layout is object, hyphen, layout name with literal spaces; EmailTemplate is
  Folder/Name with the EmailFolder as its own member; Report and Dashboard folders are bare members
  of the Report and Dashboard types; Settings is named PathAssistant because feature settings take
  no wildcard. Sources: admin/change-management-and-deployment references/metadata-examples.md
  section 1; admin/opportunity-management references/metadata-examples.md section 5;
  admin/approval-processes references/metadata-examples.md "package.xml"; admin/reports-and-dashboards
  references/metadata-examples.md section 5; admin/email-templates-and-alerts
  references/metadata-and-sender-identity.md.

  Version 62.0: every step manifest declares 62.0, plan.json carries no api_version, and the
  metadata-builder Inputs default is 62.0. M3-S03's TestDataFactory.cls-meta.xml carries 67.0 by plan
  decision D-M3S03-01; a class's own apiVersion governs its compile, and MOCK-DEPLOY-M3 run 5
  validated the set at 62.0.

  Type blocks are listed in the deploy order of deploy-order.md section 3. The platform resolves
  references inside one request whatever the block order; the order is there for a reader and for
  anyone who splits request 1 further.
-->
